# Mathematical Libraries & Core Utilities

Technical documentation for all mathematical libraries, utility functions, and shared types used throughout the MegaFi Hedge protocol.

## BlackScholes.sol - Options Pricing Mathematics

### Overview

Implements the Black-Scholes-Merton model for European options pricing and Greeks calculation. Core mathematical engine for option valuation.

### Library Structure

```solidity
library BlackScholes {
    using PRBMathSD59x18 for int256;
    using PRBMathUD60x18 for uint256;
}
```

Uses PRBMath for high-precision fixed-point arithmetic (59.18 signed, 60.18 unsigned).

### Core Pricing Functions

**Black-Scholes Formula**:
```solidity
function blackScholesCalc(
    uint256 spotPrice,      // Current underlying price
    uint256 strikePrice,    // Option strike price
    uint256 timeToExpiry,   // Time remaining in seconds
    uint256 volatility,     // Annual implied volatility (e18)
    uint256 riskFreeRate,   // Annual risk-free rate (e18)
    bool isPut              // true for put, false for call
) public pure returns (uint256 premium)
```

**Implementation**:

1. **Convert to Fixed-Point**:
```solidity
int256 S = int256(spotPrice);
int256 K = int256(strikePrice);
int256 T = int256(timeToExpiry).div(int256(365 days));  // Years
int256 sigma = int256(volatility);
int256 r = int256(riskFreeRate);
```

2. **Calculate d1 and d2**:
```solidity
// d1 = [ln(S/K) + (r + σ²/2) × T] / (σ × √T)
int256 lnSK = S.div(K).ln();  // ln(S/K)
int256 sigmaSq = sigma.mul(sigma);  // σ²
int256 numerator = lnSK.add(
    r.add(sigmaSq.div(2e18)).mul(T)
);
int256 denominator = sigma.mul(T.sqrt());
int256 d1 = numerator.div(denominator);

// d2 = d1 - σ × √T
int256 d2 = d1.sub(sigma.mul(T.sqrt()));
```

3. **Calculate N(d1) and N(d2)** (cumulative normal distribution):
```solidity
int256 Nd1 = _normalCDF(d1);
int256 Nd2 = _normalCDF(d2);
```

4. **Calculate Premium**:

For **Call Options**:
```solidity
// C = S × N(d1) - K × e^(-r×T) × N(d2)
int256 callPrice = S.mul(Nd1).sub(
    K.mul((-r.mul(T)).exp()).mul(Nd2)
);
premium = uint256(callPrice);
```

For **Put Options**:
```solidity
// P = K × e^(-r×T) × N(-d2) - S × N(-d1)
int256 putPrice = K.mul((-r.mul(T)).exp()).mul(_normalCDF(d2.neg()))
    .sub(S.mul(_normalCDF(d1.neg())));
premium = uint256(putPrice);
```

Alternative via **Put-Call Parity**:
```solidity
// P = C - S + K × e^(-r×T)
uint256 callPrice = blackScholesCalc(..., false);
int256 putPrice = int256(callPrice)
    .sub(int256(S))
    .add(K.mul((-r.mul(T)).exp()));
premium = uint256(putPrice);
```

### Greeks Calculations

**Delta (Δ)** - Price sensitivity:
```solidity
function calculateDelta(
    uint256 spotPrice,
    uint256 strikePrice,
    uint256 timeToExpiry,
    uint256 volatility,
    uint256 riskFreeRate,
    bool isPut
) public pure returns (int256 delta)
```

**Call Delta**:
```solidity
// Δ_call = N(d1)
int256 d1 = _calculateD1(spotPrice, strikePrice, timeToExpiry, volatility, riskFreeRate);
delta = _normalCDF(d1);  // Range: 0 to 1
```

**Put Delta**:
```solidity
// Δ_put = N(d1) - 1
int256 d1 = _calculateD1(...);
delta = _normalCDF(d1).sub(1e18);  // Range: -1 to 0
```

**Gamma (Γ)** - Delta sensitivity:
```solidity
function calculateGamma(
    uint256 spotPrice,
    uint256 strikePrice,
    uint256 timeToExpiry,
    uint256 volatility,
    uint256 riskFreeRate
) public pure returns (uint256 gamma)
```

**Formula**:
```solidity
// Γ = φ(d1) / (S × σ × √T)
// Where φ(d1) is the standard normal PDF

int256 d1 = _calculateD1(...);
int256 phi_d1 = _normalPDF(d1);

int256 denominator = int256(spotPrice)
    .mul(int256(volatility))
    .mul(int256(timeToExpiry).div(int256(365 days)).sqrt());

gamma = uint256(phi_d1.div(denominator));
```

Note: Gamma is the same for calls and puts with same strike/expiry.

**Theta (Θ)** - Time decay:
```solidity
function calculateTheta(
    uint256 spotPrice,
    uint256 strikePrice,
    uint256 timeToExpiry,
    uint256 volatility,
    uint256 riskFreeRate,
    bool isPut
) public pure returns (int256 theta)
```

**Call Theta**:
```solidity
// Θ_call = -(S × φ(d1) × σ) / (2 × √T) - r × K × e^(-r×T) × N(d2)

int256 d1 = _calculateD1(...);
int256 d2 = _calculateD2(...);
int256 phi_d1 = _normalPDF(d1);
int256 T_sqrt = int256(timeToExpiry).div(int256(365 days)).sqrt();

int256 term1 = int256(spotPrice)
    .mul(phi_d1)
    .mul(int256(volatility))
    .div(2e18.mul(T_sqrt));

int256 term2 = int256(riskFreeRate)
    .mul(int256(strikePrice))
    .mul((-int256(riskFreeRate).mul(T)).exp())
    .mul(_normalCDF(d2));

theta = term1.neg().sub(term2);
```

**Put Theta**:
```solidity
// Θ_put = -(S × φ(d1) × σ) / (2 × √T) + r × K × e^(-r×T) × N(-d2)

// Similar to call, but second term is positive
theta = term1.neg().add(term2_put);
```

**Vega (ν)** - Volatility sensitivity:
```solidity
function calculateVega(
    uint256 spotPrice,
    uint256 strikePrice,
    uint256 timeToExpiry,
    uint256 volatility,
    uint256 riskFreeRate
) public pure returns (uint256 vega)
```

**Formula**:
```solidity
// ν = S × φ(d1) × √T

int256 d1 = _calculateD1(...);
int256 phi_d1 = _normalPDF(d1);
int256 T_sqrt = int256(timeToExpiry).div(int256(365 days)).sqrt();

vega = uint256(
    int256(spotPrice).mul(phi_d1).mul(T_sqrt)
);
```

Note: Vega is the same for calls and puts.

**Rho (ρ)** - Interest rate sensitivity:
```solidity
function calculateRho(
    uint256 spotPrice,
    uint256 strikePrice,
    uint256 timeToExpiry,
    uint256 volatility,
    uint256 riskFreeRate,
    bool isPut
) public pure returns (int256 rho)
```

**Call Rho**:
```solidity
// ρ_call = K × T × e^(-r×T) × N(d2)

int256 d2 = _calculateD2(...);
int256 T = int256(timeToExpiry).div(int256(365 days));

rho = int256(strikePrice)
    .mul(T)
    .mul((-int256(riskFreeRate).mul(T)).exp())
    .mul(_normalCDF(d2));
```

**Put Rho**:
```solidity
// ρ_put = -K × T × e^(-r×T) × N(-d2)

rho = int256(strikePrice)
    .mul(T)
    .mul((-int256(riskFreeRate).mul(T)).exp())
    .mul(_normalCDF(d2.neg()))
    .neg();
```

### Statistical Functions

**Cumulative Normal Distribution N(x)**:
```solidity
function _normalCDF(int256 x) internal pure returns (int256)
```

Uses **Abramowitz and Stegun approximation**:
```solidity
// For x >= 0:
// N(x) ≈ 1 - φ(x) × (a₁t + a₂t² + a₃t³ + a₄t⁴ + a₅t⁵)
// Where t = 1 / (1 + p × x)

int256 a1 = 0.254829592e18;
int256 a2 = -0.284496736e18;
int256 a3 = 1.421413741e18;
int256 a4 = -1.453152027e18;
int256 a5 = 1.061405429e18;
int256 p = 0.3275911e18;

if (x >= 0) {
    int256 t = 1e18.div(1e18.add(p.mul(x)));
    int256 phi = _normalPDF(x);
    int256 poly = a1.mul(t)
        .add(a2.mul(t.mul(t)))
        .add(a3.mul(t.mul(t).mul(t)))
        .add(a4.mul(t.mul(t).mul(t).mul(t)))
        .add(a5.mul(t.mul(t).mul(t).mul(t).mul(t)));
    
    return 1e18.sub(phi.mul(poly));
} else {
    // N(-x) = 1 - N(x)
    return 1e18.sub(_normalCDF(x.neg()));
}
```

**Normal Probability Density Function φ(x)**:
```solidity
function _normalPDF(int256 x) internal pure returns (int256)
```

**Formula**:
```solidity
// φ(x) = (1 / √(2π)) × e^(-x²/2)

int256 coefficient = 0.398942280401433e18;  // 1 / √(2π)
int256 exponent = x.mul(x).div(2e18).neg();  // -x²/2

return coefficient.mul(exponent.exp());
```

